# Mesh-accelerated slab-based dispersion Ewald (pppm/disp/slab) for a planar LJ
# liquid-vapor slab -- typically the fastest accurate long-range dispersion for
# planar interfaces.  Damped only; pairs with a plain-cutoff LJ pair style.
# Here we also tabulate the long-range pressure profile with the IK contour.

units           lj
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

read_data       data.lj_slab
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (10 10 36)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  1267 atoms
  reading velocities ...
  1267 velocities
  read_data CPU = 0.006 seconds

pair_style      lj/cut 3.0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0

kspace_style    pppm/disp/slab 1.0e-3
kspace_modify   corr bin contour ik
# corr bin is auto-sized to the requested force accuracy; for very tight
# tolerances the fine bins become costly, so use corr raw (exact) instead.

variable        lz equal lz
variable        gamma equal 0.5*v_lz*(pzz-0.5*(pxx+pyy))
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press pxx pyy pzz v_gamma
thermo          50

velocity        all create 0.85 4928 mom yes
fix             1 all nve
timestep        0.004
run             500
